Subject: [PATCH] dndcp/wayland: file copy/paste

Adds CPFORMAT_FILELIST in both directions, plus DND_CP_CAP_FILE_CP. As with
the image bit, without the capability the VMX never offers the format
regardless of the handler code.

host -> guest is lazy, using the same vmblock mechanism as the X11 backend
rather than copying anything eagerly. On receiving a file list we create a
staging directory, add a vmblock on it, and publish a text/uri-list pointing
at the paths through VMBLOCK_FUSE_FS_ROOT. Nothing is transferred at this
point; the clipboard holds a few hundred bytes of paths. A monitor thread
blocks reading the corresponding path under VMBLOCK_FUSE_NOTIFY_ROOT, which
returns only when the pasting application opens one of the published files.
That is when SrcUIRequestFiles() pulls the bytes, and GetLocalFilesDone()
lifts the block so the stalled reader proceeds. Copying a large file on the
host and never pasting it therefore transfers nothing.

Any outstanding block is removed when a new clip arrives, as
CopyPasteUIX11::GetRemoteClipboardCB does. The staging directory is reused
whenever it is still empty -- the normal state after a clip is published but
never pasted -- so without this AddBlock refuses it and only the first file
paste of a session works. AddBlock is retried once after a RemoveBlock if it
still fails.

guest -> host needs no vmblock, since the host pulls the contents itself. The
local text/uri-list is parsed with DnD_UriListGetNextFile, sizes are summed
with File_GetSizeEx for SetFileSize, and the result is serialized with
DnDFileList::ToCPClipboard. Leading "copy\n" / "cut\n" markers are stripped:
KDE signals the operation out of band via application/x-kde-cutselection, but
handling both keeps one code path for GNOME too.

Both directions probe for files before image and text. A file selection also
advertises a text rendering of the paths, and consuming that would turn a file
copy into a copy of filenames.

CopyPasteDnDWayland gains the block plumbing it had no equivalent of:
ctx->blockFD (supplied by vmware-user-suid-wrapper as --blockFd) feeds
DnD_CompleteBlockInitialization, and the control block is handed to the UI in
RegisterCP. Where vmblock is unavailable, file paste is declined rather than
falling back to an eager copy.

Relative paths are percent-escaped per RFC 1630, matching
CopyPasteUIX11::GetNextPath. Unlike the X11 backend, the staging directory is
passed explicitly to SrcUIRequestFiles() instead of relying on
DnD_CreateStagingDirectory() happening to reuse the still-empty directory.

Non-file URI schemes (trash:, recent:) are skipped rather than resolved. The
X11 backend resolves them with GFile; this backend deliberately links no Gtk
stack, and ordinary file managers put file:// URIs on the clipboard.

Verified on Bazzite 44 (Fedora 44, KDE Plasma 6 Wayland), open-vm-tools
13.1.0, VMware Workstation 26H2: copy/paste capabilities resolve to 0x515,
single and multi-file transfers land intact in both directions (16.4 MiB
archive verified), and nothing transfers until the paste.
---
